  "description": "Within one direction a recording's stamps never decrease, across a core restart included (phase-01; x-compare). Each stamp keeps its owner: the worker keeps each session's output stamps non-decreasing at the source — a clock that steps back stamps the previous value, so output 2 shares output 1's stamp — and the core never alters one; the core keeps its own input stamps non-decreasing. Across directions nothing is assumed: here input is stamped before output that precedes it, by another clock. Refused: an output stamp that goes back, an input stamp that goes back, and a gap marker stamped before the output it follows (it belongs to the output clock).",
